{{> person}}

Find public mentions of the person in their professional role from the last 24 months, newest first, at most 8: news articles, interviews, press releases, podcasts, conference talks and publications.
For each give the headline and its publication date (YYYY-MM-DD, or null when the page doesn't show it), with the page itself as the source.
The headline must tell the news on its own: readers will see only the headline and the date, not the page. Use the published title when it does. When it is vague, such as "Episode 42" or "Keynote session", write a one-sentence headline that says what the person did or said instead. If you can't find that, skip the page.
Skip pages that only list the person's name, such as directories, staff lists and event attendee lists.

